  "analytic_review": {
    "native_operator": "Archived native representation has at most8 offdiagonal entries per role and one full diagonal. n_total128, |m|<20, |c0|,|d|<6, |rho|<=128. ci radical <=(n+1)/2; sqrt2 times CG f <=sqrt(n(n+3))<n+2<=128. The deliberately looser 2*6*128 per offdiagonal and 16 total entries give symmetric row/column bound1078272<2^22. Integer radicands are below2^53; positive formation paths fit gamma64. Captured coefficient errors<2^-48 give operator error6*n_total*2^-48=768*2^-48 by the norm2 one-particle generators, not a pointwise current cap. Numba full_action covers all rows and exterior in this invariant selected space.",
    "sigma": "Exact rational recomputation gives action_error5.029642318925349e-8<2^-24. Coefficient formation+gamma40 action accumulation+4u(2^22+|mu|) subtraction+100D*2^-1074+2*2^-490 covers native H-muq action. gamma(2D+8)=2418081/1125899904424543\u22482.147687366e-9. Squared-norm underflow is amplified by sqrt; the2*2^-490 allowance dominates the amplified errors. Source-normalization and residual reductions are enclosed by1/(1-4gamma). (computed residual+action_error)/(1-4gamma)=1.0708703667410749e-7<sigma2^-22. The recovered observed source norm1+2^-52 and its outward defect make this denominator safe; unnormalized-residual inference alone would be wrong.",
    "normalization_denominator": "The new CLI independently checks norm_defect<2gamma and (1-norm_defect)(1-2gamma)>1-4gamma. Since exact ||v||>=1-norm_defect, this protects the normalized residual ratio including the source denominator; it is not a floating Ritz upper claim. Inverting the norm-defect formula has two sign branches. The positive branch is observed_float_norm=1+2^-52; the negative branch has a non-dyadic denominator and cannot be a finite binary64 scalar. Recovery is scalar consistency, not independent full-vector measurement.",
    "unique_ground_and_projection": "For normalized exact binary u=v/||v||, ||(H-muq)u||<=sigma. Rayleigh E in[muq-sigma,muq+sigma] lies below beta=-5123<=lambda2. Temple gives E0>=muq-sigma-sigma\u00b2/g, E0<=muq+sigma, g=beta-(muq+sigma)=1502586528801/1099511627776>1. Thus |E0-muq|<=sigma+sigma\u00b2/g and excited weight<=sigma\u00b2/g\u00b2. p=sigma/g is UNSQUARED source spectral projection error/sin-angle; upper-ground earlier1.2467e-10 remains infidelity only. Since Rayleigh below beta and lambda2>=beta, selected ground is unique. Whole P0, not density-zero, is rank one.",
    "lift": "A0=H-E0+P0>=I. Atilde=H-muq+vv^T is the exact mathematical operator approximated by the numerical matvec, not the binary assembled matrix interpreted as exact H. With eta=| ||v||\u00b2-1 |<=norm_defect, ||Atilde-A0||<=|E0-muq|+2p+eta=deltaA5.89489974214883e-7; the true projector difference is<=p so2p is conservative. Atilde>=(1-deltaA)I. Both energy shift and Pi replacement are selected-local only.",
    "source": "Choose ground sign so ||u-Omega||<=sqrt2*p. ||Q_u rho u-Q0 rho Omega|| <=128*(sqrt2+1)*p<384p. Scaling u to exact binary v adds a norm-defect term bounded by1024eta for eta<.001. Rounded rho*v, mean contraction and mean*v subtraction add<=512gamma, including integer-rho multiplication and |rho|<=128. Hence ||b_binary-Q0rhoOmega||<=delta_b7.029219188387624e-5. The approximate mean-subtracted b is NOT itself a true ground projection; the full discrepancy is priced. Actual weight .641876... with huge margin gives ||b_binary||<=1 even after subnormal allowance.",
    "dot_and_solve": "Recovered scalar xnorm_upper\u2248.00457431229004605, derived with the outward norm factor, is<1. Exact Atilde-action error<=action_error+16gamma, including native coefficients, mu subtraction and approximate rank-one dot/vector formation. Exact solve residual upper4.382979781919084e-10 includes residual norm rounding, action error*xnorm_upper and final b-ax rounding u(1+2^23*xnorm_upper). For fixed exact binary x, V=2<b,x>-<x,Atilde x> satisfies <b,Atilde^-1 b>-V=<r,Atilde^-1 r> in[0,||r||\u00b2/Amin]. The computed floating form is enclosed by gamma*(2+2^23*xnorm_upper\u00b2)+lifted_action_error*xnorm_upper\u00b2+underflow=3.8127217585679244e-7. gamma2D+8 has room for dot multiplication/reduction and final arithmetic. Attempt2 unpriced1e-7 is not used. CG convergence is not the proof; the paid residual is.",
    "inverse": "||Atilde^-1||<=1/Amin and ||A0^-1||<=1. Resolvent identity gives ||Atilde^-1-A0^-1||<=deltaA/Amin, NOT a missing Amin^-2: the exact inverse has norm<=1. Insertion plus inverse discrepancy is safely bounded by2delta_b(1+delta_b)/Amin+(1+delta_b)\u00b2deltaA/Amin=.00014118392182895092. Exact scalar recomputation reproduces both alpha endpoints and outward reversed curvature endpoints.",
    "contact_and_coupling": "Native Block diagonal64(rho+s)\u00b2 gives Hprime(0)=128rho and Hsecond(0)=128I. Isolated selected-ground perturbation theory gives Esecond(0)=128-2*128\u00b2*<Q0rhoOmega,(H-E0)^-1Q0rhoOmega>=128-32768alpha. A sign change of the linear coupling leaves its square unchanged, but changing the negative second-order energy correction or halving contact is wrong. This is a finite selected-sector analytic ground derivative, not dielectric-to-bulk promotion.",
    "diagnostics_and_corrections": "No mathematical correction is required for the stated local curvature interval under its assumptions. Preserve explicit model and scope. The first/current moments are unpriced float diagnostics; no certified exact-moment or pole claim follows. The complete_projected_resolvent_residual_float field measures the approximate lifted solve, not the exact-ground resolvent residual; proof separately prices its discrepancy. Keeping xnorm_float and source_norm_squared_float explicitly in a future receipt would improve provenance, but neither is needed as a new theorem assumption: their exact values/bounds are recoverable from current rational budgets. No pointwise/unbounded-current cap, global or moment promotion survives this review."
